    {
      "id": "zoom-level-floor-ceiling-model-goal",
      "type": "goal",
      "label": "Level selection follows content size and allotted space, not full-window occupancy",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": -160
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 300,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "top",
          "label": "top",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 270
        },
        {
          "id": "bottom",
          "label": "bottom",
          "direction": "output",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 90
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "outcome": "A view is selected because it fits the room this instance actually has, at a size that is actually legible — never because it crosses a fixed percentage of the full browser window.",
        "priority": "high",
        "status": "todo",
        "owner": "Michael",
        "definitionKey": "goal",
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "goal",
          "sourceRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/goal.node-class.node",
          "ref": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/goal.node-class.node"
        },
        "_bridge": {
          "sourceBridgeNodeId": "zoom-level-floor-ceiling-model-bridge-goal",
          "sourceRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/goal.node-class.node",
          "classKey": "goal",
          "classRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/goal.node-class.node"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "zoom-level-floor-ceiling-model-declaration"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "zoom-level-floor-ceiling-model-task-natural-size",
      "type": "task",
      "label": "1 — Give every named view its own natural size",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": -1550,
        "y": 260
      },
      "width": 430,
      "height": 300,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "top",
          "label": "top",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 270
        },
        {
          "id": "bottom",
          "label": "bottom",
          "direction": "output",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 90
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "body": "Build one size-probe that measures each rank's intrinsic size from whatever is actually there — a view's own size for authored content, or (recursively) a referenced graph's own natural size at that same rank for a delegated/portal view or the un-authored raw-nodes fallback — instead of a per-level fixed box or the graph's full content extent. Nobody declares a size; rendering order (which rank) is what's authored, size is measured from it.\n\nBuilt: the general resolver contract (representationResolver.js), the referenced-graph half of the size-probe (intrinsicSize.js: graphIntrinsicSize, wrapping graphRenderBounds()), and the authored-content half (intrinsicSize.js: viewIntrinsicSize) — turns out this doesn't need a DOM measurement pass after all: a view node's own width/height already is its intrinsic size claim, the same way any node's size is however big it was left after editing, not a separately-declared number. createDefaultViewNode() now gives icon and summary their LEVEL_BOX_SIZE dimensions instead of a uniform 420x300 for every level, so a fresh graph's summary view genuinely is summary-sized. Confirmed live in a test: a brand-new graph's summary view resolves to summary rank in a typical starting workspace slot (400x300), with no special-cased creation-time ceiling override needed — per Michael: \"we make the new graph template have a view that renders at the size we want.\" All unit-tested (tests/representationResolver.test.js, tests/intrinsicSize.test.js, tests/systemNodeDefaultsViewSize.test.js). Not yet wired into live rendering — presentWorkspaceInstances and resolveWorkspacePresentationLevel are untouched; that's task 3.\n\nA DOM-measurement refinement (for authored content whose width/height was never touched from whatever default created it) remains a possible future pass, but the contract doesn't need it to work today.\n\nAlso fixed along the way: graphExtent() (graphWorkspace.js) and defaultMembraneBounds() (membraneGeometry.js) both floored a graph's natural size at 640x480 regardless of actual content. Removed from both — confirmed harmless: createDefaultGraph() and every real template/graph checked already produce 1700-3900px natural extents from their own real content. A synthetic small idea card now correctly measures its own content + padding instead of being forced to 640x480.",
        "priority": "medium",
        "status": "done",
        "owner": "Michael",
        "definitionKey": "task",
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "task",
          "sourceRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/task.node-class.node",
          "ref": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/task.node-class.node"
        },
        "_bridge": {
          "sourceBridgeNodeId": "zoom-level-floor-ceiling-model-bridge-task",
          "sourceRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/task.node-class.node",
          "classKey": "task",
          "classRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/task.node-class.node"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "zoom-level-floor-ceiling-model-declaration"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "zoom-level-floor-ceiling-model-task-allotted-space",
      "type": "task",
      "label": "2 — Compute the space actually allotted to each instance",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": -880,
        "y": 260
      },
      "width": 430,
      "height": 300,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "top",
          "label": "top",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 270
        },
        {
          "id": "bottom",
          "label": "bottom",
          "direction": "output",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 90
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "body": "Stop comparing against window.innerWidth/innerHeight for every instance alike. A collapsed workspace card sharing room with several siblings has less space than a focused graph alone on screen — the ceiling needs to reflect that, not the full window.",
        "priority": "medium",
        "status": "todo",
        "owner": "Michael",
        "definitionKey": "task",
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "task",
          "sourceRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/task.node-class.node",
          "ref": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/task.node-class.node"
        },
        "_bridge": {
          "sourceBridgeNodeId": "zoom-level-floor-ceiling-model-bridge-task",
          "sourceRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/task.node-class.node",
          "classKey": "task",
          "classRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/task.node-class.node"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "zoom-level-floor-ceiling-model-declaration"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "zoom-level-floor-ceiling-model-task-selector",
      "type": "task",
      "label": "3 — Replace occupancy-driven selection with floor/ceiling",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": -210,
        "y": 260
      },
      "width": 430,
      "height": 300,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "top",
          "label": "top",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 270
        },
        {
          "id": "bottom",
          "label": "bottom",
          "direction": "output",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 90
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "body": "Retune resolveWorkspacePresentationLevel, occupancyResolution, and resolvePercentageGraphView (or their eventual unification, per semantic-zoom-architecture) to pick the largest view whose natural size × zoom does not exceed the allotted-space ceiling, among views at or above the legibility floor.",
        "priority": "medium",
        "status": "todo",
        "owner": "Michael",
        "definitionKey": "task",
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "task",
          "sourceRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/task.node-class.node",
          "ref": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/task.node-class.node"
        },
        "_bridge": {
